# The built apworld IS tracked: it is what people download and drop into
# Archipelago's custom_worlds folder. Rebuild it with tools/build_apworld.py
# and commit the result whenever the world changes.

# Generated multiworlds and spoilers
/output/

# Reverse-engineering tooling: memory scanners, disassembly helpers, RTTI and
# archive readers, and the one-off probes used to find the addresses written up
# in notes/REVERSE.md. None of it is part of the apworld.
#
# The contents are ignored rather than the directory itself, because git cannot
# un-ignore a file inside an ignored directory.
/tools/*
/tools/data/*
/tools/snapshots/

# ...except what this repository cannot rebuild itself without.
#
# Four modules under world/empire_earth are generated, and these are the only
# things that can regenerate them - two of them from a *running game*, which is
# not something a contributor could reconstruct by reading the source. The
# build and the test suite are here for the same reason: without them there is
# no way to package the world, or to tell whether a seed is winnable.
!/tools/build_apworld.py
!/tools/test_generation.py

# -> world/empire_earth/Objects.py        buildings, units, wonders
!/tools/gen_objects.py
# -> world/empire_earth/Producers.py      which building makes which unit
!/tools/gen_producers.py
# -> world/empire_earth/Technologies.py   needs Empire Earth open, in a match
!/tools/gen_technologies.py
# -> world/empire_earth/BuildingEpochs.py needs Empire Earth open, in a match
!/tools/gen_building_epochs.py
# -> world/empire_earth/UnitSlots.py      from the menu listings in tools/data
!/tools/build_unit_slots.py
# -> world/empire_earth/UnitIcons.py      needs Empire Earth open, in a match
!/tools/gen_unit_slots.py
# -> world/empire_earth/TechUnlocks.py    needs Empire Earth open, in a match
!/tools/gen_tech_unlocks.py
# -> world/empire_earth/Upgrades.py       which unit replaces which
!/tools/gen_upgrades.py

# Holds Archipelago's connect handshake open so the connect race can be
# reproduced on demand. Without it that bug only shows up in a busy room.
!/tools/race_probe.py

# Libraries the above import.
!/tools/blast.py
!/tools/dbobjects.py
!/tools/eemem.py
!/tools/install.py
!/tools/ssa_extract.py

# The wiki's technology list, joined against the running game to build
# Technologies.py. Not derivable from anything else in the repository.
!/tools/data/
!/tools/data/technologies.tsv

# Every build menu, read off a vanilla game by hand across all fifteen epochs.
# The only source UnitSlots.py has — three attempts to derive it from memory
# gave tables that looked right and weren't. Losing these means doing it again.
!/tools/data/*_slots.tsv

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# Editor / OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
